<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Flatters expedition</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1880–1881</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Flatters expedition was a French mission led by Lieutenant-Colonel Paul Flatters to survey a route for a railway across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>. On its second journey in February 1881 it was attacked by Kel Ahaggar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuareg">Tuareg</a> in the Ahaggar region; Flatters and most of the party were killed. The disaster halted French plans for the central Sahara for some two decades.</p></div>
